I can add a data point to this: the same issue still reproduces on a
kernel that already contains the three fixes referenced above.

Hardware:
  GPU: AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT 16GB
  CPU: Ryzen 7 9700X
  Board: ASUS TUF GAMING B850M-PLUS WIFI, BIOS 1681 (06/18/2026)

Software:
  Debian 13 (trixie), kernel 7.1.8-1~bpo13+1 (upstream 7.1.8)
  GNOME Shell / mutter, Wayland; Mesa 25.0.7-2+deb13u1;
  firmware-amd-graphics 20260622-1~bpo13+1

Upstream 7.1.8 includes via stable:
  - 8382cd234981 ("drm/amd/display: consolidate DCN vblank/flip
    handling onto vupdate_no_lock")
  - "drm/amd/display: check GRPH_FLIP status before sending event"
  - Revert of "drm/amd/display: Restore 5s vbl offdelay for NV3x+ DGPUs"

Yet I still get the same flip_done / commit wait timeouts, always at
low GPU load (desktop use, mouse movement), never under 3D load.

Observations:
- Nothing precedes the first flip_done error in the journal - no SMU
or DMCUB errors. Only the display pipeline hangs; audio and
  background processes keep running, VT switching works but takes ~10s
per step (each commit waiting out its timeout).
- The VT switch triggers an untainted WARN at
drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c:10007 in
  dm_arm_vblank_event() via amdgpu_dm_atomic_commit_tail (full trace attached).
- Reproduces on both HDMI and DisplayPort, same CRTC/plane.
- amdgpu.dcdebugmask=0x10 and 0x12 made no difference. VRR is not
enabled in mutter.
- Given the reverted offdelay workaround targeted "intermittent
flip-done timeouts on cursor updates" on dGPUs with idle
  optimizations, and my trigger profile is exactly desktop/cursor
activity at idle, could DCN 4.x have a case the new vupdate_no_lock
  path doesn't cover?

Currently testing power_dpm_force_performance_level=high as a
workaround and can follow up with results. Happy to test patches.

journal excerpt attached.

